# [LAMPS](../wg/lamps.html)

## Summary

The Limited Additional Mechanisms for PKIX and S/MIME (LAMPS) Working Group met at IETF 127 to review document progress and discuss technical updates across several active drafts, proposed specifications, and post-quantum cryptography (PQC) transitions. 

Key outcomes included progressing `draft-ietf-lamps-one-signature-certs` and `draft-ietf-lamps-attestation-freshness` toward Working Group Last Call, agreeing to remove `eFrodoKEM` from `draft-ietf-lamps-frodokem-certificates`, simplifying S/MIMEv5 requirements in `draft-ietf-lamps-rfc8550bis` and `draft-ietf-lamps-rfc8551bis` (including plans to drop CBC mode, legacy RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 where appropriate, and Zlib compression), and advancing security fixes for RFC 3161 timestamping to mitigate cross-protocol attacks. The working group also reviewed proposals for OpenID Connect authentication context types in certificates and Embedded Alternate Issuer Certificates ("Turducken / PQ Opt-Out Certificates") to facilitate WebPKI migration to PQC.

